  "term": "optic tract",
  "definition": "The optic tract is a bundle of nerve fibers that continues from the optic chiasm and carries visual information onward, mainly to the lateral geniculate bodies. It is part of the visual pathway transmitting signals that began in the retina and traveled through the optic nerves.",
